{"type":"npc","name":"Thananycti","folder":null,"system":{"attributes":{"hp":{"value":440,"temp":0,"max":440,"details":""},"ac":{"value":42,"details":""},"allSaves":{"value":""},"speed":{"value":15,"otherSpeeds":[{"type":"fly","value":60}],"details":""},"immunities":[{"type":"death-effects","exceptions":[]},{"type":"disease","exceptions":[]}],"weaknesses":[{"type":"cold-iron","value":15,"exceptions":[]}],"resistances":[{"type":"void","value":15,"exceptions":[],"doubleVs":[]}]},"initiative":{"statistic":"perception"},"details":{"languages":{"value":["chthonian","common","diabolic","empyrean","fey","melodian","necril","requian"],"details":""},"level":{"value":19},"blurb":"","publicNotes":"<p>A thananycti cloak themselves in the trappings of psychopomps, calling out to lost souls with a soft, sorrowful melody, beckoning them to rest. But this is merely a ruse, utilizing their masterful lies and fey magic to conceal their true intentions—trapping the soul and fusing them into the thananycti itself.</p><h2>Soul Games</h2><p>Thananycti enjoy building elaborate charades, earning acclaim and veneration from settlements for removing restless and dangerous spirits. But as the souls of both the dead and the living begin to disappear, questions often arise, and those asking those questions often disappear as well. Eventually, they lose interest in the charade, and they shift their strategies, launching a campaign of terror and bloodshed that culminates only when no survivors remain to share the story.</p><h2>Suggested Monster Parts</h2><p><strong>Monster Parts</strong> 5,000/12,000/22,500 gp</p><p><strong>Eligible Refinements</strong> weapons (piercing, slashing), armor (light), perception item, skill items (Acrobatics, Arcana, Deception, Diplomacy, Occultism, Performance, Religion)</p><p><strong>Eligible Imbued Properties</strong> bane, charisma, death, energy resistant (vitality, void), life, lifeward armor, mind, mind shield, music, sensory (darkvision, scent, true seeing), 